course: dictionary
lesson: 2864
title: Domestication: taming over generations
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Domestication is a long word, but it has a clear meaning. It is the long process by which people tamed wild animals and plants over many generations, so they came to live with people or be farmed by them. Look at the clues in the example: «Training teaches one animal tricks in its lifetime; taming, or domestication, means people choose the calmest animals to have babies, generation after generation.» The word «taming» sits right next to it, so the sentence tells you it means the same kind of thing: making something gentle enough to live with people.
explain: The key clue is the time: «generation after generation». Training is quick and only works on one animal during its life. Domestication is slow. People pick the calmest animals to have babies, then they do it again with the next generation, and again, until the whole kind has changed. A generation is one step in a family line, like a parent and then their children.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try: «Taming means people choose the calmest animals to have babies, generation after generation.» It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Domestication means the long process of taming wild animals and plants over many generations.
fact: Domestication takes many generations, but training works within one animal's lifetime.
fact: Dogs came from wolves through domestication.
fact: Cows, sheep, wheat and rice were all domesticated long ago, in the time of the first farmers.
fact: Breeders choose the animals or plants with the features they want, and those features are passed on to the next generation.
exercise: «Taming, or domestication, means people choose the calmest animals to have babies.» What is domestication? | A wild animal running free in the forest | A kind of food grown on a farm | *A long process of taming wild animals over many generations | A quick trick an animal learns in one day
exercise: Which of these was domesticated by people long ago? | Ocean tides | *Sheep | Lightning | Thunder
exercise: «Training teaches one animal tricks in its lifetime.» Why is training different from domestication? | They mean exactly the same thing | Training is only for dogs | Domestication happens in one afternoon | *Training happens in one animal's lifetime, but domestication takes many generations
test: Which word means a long process of taming wild animals and plants over many generations? | Extinction | Training | *Domestication | Migration
test: Which two plants were domesticated long ago? | Roses and ferns | Stone and sand | Sun and moon | *Wheat and rice
exam: Which statement about domestication is true? | *Traits change slowly as calm animals have babies over many generations | Plants cannot be domesticated | Domestication is the same as hunting wild animals | Animals are domesticated with one trick learned in one lifetime
